---
import { weekByNumber } from '../data/curriculum';
import { withBase } from 'astro-theme-university/url';
import AcademyScene from './AcademyScene.astro';
import FieldOperation from './FieldOperation.astro';
import { labOperation, labOperations } from '../data/lab-operations';
import { labRequiresEnactment, observationFacts, memoryItems, loci, archiveFiles, councilClaims, initialPlan } from '../lib/training-engine';
import '../styles/training.css';
import '../styles/learner-guidance.css';
import {labGuides} from '../data/learner-guidance';
interface Props { week:number }
const {week}=Astro.props;
const lesson=weekByNumber(week);
const guide=labGuides[week]!;
const fieldSpec=labOperation(week);
const operation=labOperations[week]!;
const enacted=labRequiresEnactment(week);
const directions=[
  'Inspect four scene objects, classify five statements, then choose a follow-up investigation and a conclusion supported by its result.',
  'Compare unaided recall, location cues and written notes, then select a strategy suited to the stated use.',
  'Rotate a module and change its level to match two connector directions and a specified floor.',
  'Use an inspection to diagnose the original mechanism fault before changing it; predict and verify the corrected output.',
  'Measure a six-volt training circuit, isolate its first open component, switch off, replace it and verify the lamp.',
  'Compare archive versions against a signed manifest. Select the complete copy whose checksum matches the stated deliverable.',
  'Repair an explicit role-permission matrix and test every permitted and forbidden role/action combination.',
  'Exchange a destination, quantity and verification code between analyst and operator, then confirm a readback.',
  'Check three people’s claims against records and negotiate an agreement that meets the published mandate.',
  'Choose a route objective, predict contacts, plan and execute a route that meets its conditions, and explain a trade-off.',
  'Preserve the supplied plan, expose a disruption and explain a revised sequence without overwriting Version 1.',
  'Complete a run of Operation Last Light, then connect the observed result to your objective and a credible alternative.',
];
const examples=[
  '“The door is open” reports a visible condition. “Someone escaped through it” proposes a cause. The second needs evidence beyond the first. A note saying someone left is a claim, even though the note itself is visible.',
  'Imagine an oversized compass drawing circles across the Atrium floor. At the Fountain, imagine a lantern glowing underwater. A useful association connects both place and item; simply rereading the list does not create a retrieval cue.',
  'A north/east connector rotated clockwise 90° faces east/south. Raising it from level 0 to level 1 changes position, while its connector directions stay the same.',
  'In a different training rig, a 10-tooth driver and 30-tooth follower turn six inputs into two opposite outputs. When it stalls, an inspection reveals a misaligned cam datum. Repositioning that cam restores motion. This teaches a diagnostic method; your assigned rig may have a different fault.',
  'An alternate model has a 4 V supply and two connectors. One reads 4 V and the next 0 V, narrowing the break to the segment between them. A 0 V reading alone would not distinguish a failed supply from that segment. Isolated continuity offers a second way to test the explanation.',
  'Archive B has a later timestamp than A, but its checksum differs from the signed source manifest. Recency explains sequence; the manifest states which contents are required. A later authorised amendment can change that requirement.',
  'An observer may read but cannot service or certify. Removing those extra permissions fixes two failures. Also test that read still works: blocking every action would violate the mandate.',
  '“Send those over there” omits both destination and quantity. “Send two sealed units to Relay; confirmation AMBER” can be read back and checked. The receiver must acknowledge the same details.',
  'In a different case, a museum can lend a scan today or offer supervised access tomorrow. The first serves speed; the second preserves direct inspection. Both can be feasible if custody, verification and responsibilities are explicit. A feasible agreement still has costs someone must accept.',
  'A path that enters two marked cells has two sensor contacts, even if it later leaves coverage. A plan that predicts those contacts is better specified than one that simply labels the path “safe”.',
  'If the east passage closes, crossing it earlier is no longer an available solution. A west-passage revision must include its extra relay check and identify who will verify it. Keep the old dependency visible for comparison.',
  'A recovered file is an output. Demonstrating that it is the required file needs the integrity checks in the mission record. If the objective changed, explain when and why instead of rewriting the initial objective.',
];
---
<section class="training-lab" data-training-week={week} data-mission-url={withBase('/operation/')} aria-labelledby={'training-title-'+week}>
  <header class="training-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">FIELD TRAINING / {String(week).padStart(2,'0')}</p>
    <h2 id={'training-title-'+week}>{lesson.title}</h2>
    <p class="intro"><strong>{operation.title}.</strong> {operation.objective}</p>
    <p>{operation.problem}</p>
    <p><strong>The skill you need:</strong> {directions[week-1]}</p>
    <p class="small"><strong>Evidence output:</strong> {lesson.output}. <strong>Later use:</strong> {lesson.missionUse}</p>
  </header>
  <details class="training-learn" data-immersive-panel="worked-example" open>
    <summary>Learn the skill · worked example</summary>
    <p>{examples[week-1]}</p>
    <p>First explain what you predict. Manipulate the apparatus, compare the observed result, then change one relevant condition. The transfer challenge changes the context so that repeating an earlier answer may fail.</p>
  </details>
  <p class="learner-orientation"><strong>Start here:</strong> read the worked example, then use the controls in <strong>Practice</strong>. {enacted?'After verifying the skill, apply it at the mission station and confirm its physical consequence.':'The completed investigation, experiment or agreement is your practical output. The field operation is an optional narrative extension.'} Then try <strong>Skill check</strong> and <strong>Transfer challenge</strong>. The six rows in the lab timetable describe the whole teaching session; they are not six hidden game levels.</p>
  <AcademyScene room={String(week)} week={week} mode="lab" />
  <div data-immersive-panel="lab">
  {enacted?<FieldOperation spec={fieldSpec} scope={'lab:'+week} />:<details data-optional-field-extension><summary>Optional field extension · act on your result</summary><p>Your lab record does not require this transport and handover sequence. Use it to rehearse the result in the academy story.</p><FieldOperation spec={fieldSpec} scope={'lab:'+week} /></details>}
  <section class="learner-guide" aria-labelledby={'lab-mission-'+week}>
    <p class="eyebrow">LAB MISSION / <span data-guidance-phase>Practice</span></p>
    <h3 id={'lab-mission-'+week}>What you are trying to do</h3>
    <p>{guide.goal}</p>
    <div class="learner-next"><p class="eyebrow">DO THIS NEXT</p><p data-lab-next role="status" aria-live="polite">{guide.steps[0]!.action}</p></div>
    <details class="learner-checklist" open>
      <summary>Equipment instructions for this mission</summary>
      <ol data-lab-checklist>{guide.steps.map((step,i)=><li data-lab-step={i}><strong>{step.title}</strong><p>{step.action}</p></li>)}</ol>
    </details>
    <p class="small"><strong>How you know you are done:</strong> {guide.success} {enacted?'Then enact the verified intervention at the mission station and confirm its consequence.':'Save the practical record and your explanation; no package delivery is required.'}</p>
    {week===1&&<details class="learner-vocabulary" open><summary>Observation, claim and inference — in plain words</summary><dl><dt>Observation</dt><dd>A detail you directly see or measure: “The door is open.”</dd><dt>Claim</dt><dd>Something a person or document tells you: “I left first.” It may be true, but the statement alone does not verify it.</dd><dt>Inference</dt><dd>An explanation you draw from evidence: “Someone left in a hurry.” An open door alone does not establish that explanation.</dd></dl><p>For the note, classify the <strong>message it asserts</strong>. Seeing that a note exists is an observation; believing its message is a separate question.</p></details>}
    <p class="small"><strong>Inspect</strong> means select a named object and read its finding. <strong>Use the equipment</strong> means operate the labelled controls below, then check the result. Exploring the scene does not automatically complete the task.</p>
  </section>
  <div class="training-legend"><span>01 · Briefing</span><span>02 · Investigate</span><span>03 · Verify</span><span>04 · Act</span><span>05 · Handover</span></div>
  <p class="small">The apparatus and the controls below use the same model. All tasks can be completed with keyboard controls. {week===1?'Inspect the four objects and test an explanation with a further record. Covering the scene for recall is optional. ':week===2?'Compare three disclosed retrieval methods. Accuracy is evidence to discuss, not a perfect-score gate. ':''}No timer is required.</p>
  <div class="training-phase" role="group" aria-label="Choose a training configuration">
    <button type="button" data-training-phase="practice" aria-pressed="true" disabled>Practice</button>
    <button type="button" data-training-phase="check" aria-pressed="false" disabled>Skill check</button>
    <button type="button" data-training-phase="transfer" aria-pressed="false" disabled>Transfer challenge</button>
  </div>
  <div data-training-controls class="training-controls"><p>The complete worksheet below is available while the interactive lab loads.</p></div>
  <div class="actions">
    <button type="button" data-training-test disabled>{week===12?'Verify completed run and account':week===11?'Verify revised plan and rehearsal':'Test this configuration'}</button>
    <button type="button" data-training-reset disabled>Restart this phase</button>
    <button type="button" data-training-hint disabled>Reveal next hint</button>
  </div>
  <div class="training-feedback">
    <p data-training-result class="eyebrow">Practice in progress</p>
    <p data-training-feedback role="status" aria-live="polite">Load the controls or use the worksheet to begin.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="training-hints">
    {lesson.hints.map((text:string,i:number)=><p data-training-hint-text hidden><strong>Hint {i+1}.</strong> {text}</p>)}
  </div>
  <section data-immersive-reflection class="learner-after" aria-labelledby={'training-after-'+week}>
  <h3 id={'training-after-'+week}>After playing · explain and save this attempt</h3>
  <p data-lab-after-message class="small">Finish the practical attempt first. Then record what you noticed, what changed and any help you used. You can also preserve an unfinished attempt.</p>
  <label for={'training-reflection-'+week}>Explain your prediction, the result you observed and what changed in your understanding.</label>
  <textarea id={'training-reflection-'+week} data-training-reflection rows="4" maxlength="4000" placeholder="Use a specific observation from your attempt. What would you test next?"></textarea>
  <div class="actions"><button type="button" class="primary" data-training-save disabled>Record attempt in skills passport</button></div>
  <p data-training-save-status role="status" class="small">Recording preserves your actions and explanation. Practice feedback does not award an academic grade.</p>
  <details><summary>Your recent action trace</summary><ol data-training-trace class="training-trace"><li>No actions recorded yet.</li></ol></details>
  </section>
  <dialog data-training-confirm-dialog aria-labelledby={'training-confirm-title-'+week} aria-describedby={'training-confirm-message-'+week}>
    <h2 id={'training-confirm-title-'+week}>Replace the current activity attempt?</h2>
    <p id={'training-confirm-message-'+week} data-training-confirm-message>Export or record this attempt first to keep its evidence. Your saved passport records remain available.</p>
    <div class="actions"><button type="button" data-training-confirm-cancel autofocus>Keep this attempt</button><button type="button" data-training-confirm-accept>Continue</button></div>
  </dialog>
  </div>
  <details class="training-worksheet" data-immersive-panel="worksheet">
    <summary>Complete worksheet and explanation · works without JavaScript</summary>
    <p><strong>Mission:</strong> {operation.objective}</p><p><strong>Obstacle:</strong> {operation.problem}</p><p><strong>Task:</strong> {directions[week-1]}</p><p><strong>{enacted?'Practical enactment:':'Optional field extension:'}</strong> once the equipment check passes, {operation.actionLabel.toLowerCase()}. Trace the result through {operation.checkpoints.join(' → ')}, then {operation.resolveLabel.toLowerCase()}. Expected consequence: {operation.consequence}</p>
    {week===1&&<><h3>Observation and investigation worksheet</h3><ul>{observationFacts.practice.map(f=><li>{f.label}</li>)}</ul><p>Inspect and classify the statements. Then compare competing explanations: hurried departure or a scheduled delivery? You may request the delivery booking and door record, or inspect the cup colour again. The booking starts at 08:10 and the door opens at 08:12; neither record identifies the person. Explain what that evidence supports and leaves unresolved.</p><p>Check: routine inspection is logged before a door closes, but the note claiming the sample is intact is unverified. Transfer: supply loss is recorded at 14:02, hatch opening at 14:07. Choose a useful follow-up and bound the conclusion. Recall is optional.</p></>}
    {week===2&&<><h3>Compare retrieval strategies</h3><p>{loci.join(' → ')}</p><ul>{Object.entries(memoryItems).map(([phase,items])=><li><strong>{phase}:</strong> {items.join(', ')}.</li>)}</ul><p>Record a covered unaided attempt, a location-cue attempt and an attempt using a written record. Count correct items and preserve errors. Repeated exposure makes this a practice comparison, not a controlled experiment. Completion requires the comparison, not perfect recall.</p><p>Select a strategy for each use: a short hands-occupied briefing; an audited handover tomorrow; a temporary record outage followed by reconciliation. Explain why a cue can help temporarily while a durable record serves other people and later checks.</p></>}
    {week===3&&<><h3>Supplied module</h3><p>The initial ports face north and east at level 0. Practice target: east/south, level 0. Skill check: south/west, level 1. Transfer: west/north, level 2. Draw each original and rotated view; name where the north port ends up.</p><p><strong>Explanation:</strong> clockwise rotations are 90°, 180° and 270° respectively. The original north port becomes east, south and west. Raising the module does not change these directions.</p></>}
    {week===4&&<><h3>Mechanism diagnostic worksheet</h3><p>Output = driver teeth ÷ follower teeth × input turns; meshed gears turn oppositely. A released brake, attached return spring and specified cam datum permit motion. Available inspections reveal the brake, spring, cam datum or tooth counts. Choose the inspection that separates your candidate explanations and record a diagnosis before changing parts.</p><ul><li>Practice: 12-tooth driver, four input turns, target two outputs, datum 180°. Inspection card: brake engaged, spring attached, cam 180°, follower 24 teeth.</li><li>Check: four input turns, target four outputs, datum 180°. Inspection card: brake released, spring attached, cam 180°, follower 24 teeth.</li><li>Transfer: six input turns, target two outputs, datum 90°. Inspection card: brake released, spring absent, cam 90°, follower 36 teeth.</li></ul><p>Use the observed condition to identify a fault; correct it and compare actual output with your prediction. These are raw inspection readings, not a completed diagnosis.</p></>}
    {week===5&&<><h3>Circuit investigation worksheet</h3><details><summary>Supplied measurement cards for the static route</summary><p>Practice powered readings: battery 6 V, fuse 0 V, cable 0 V, lamp 0 V. Check: battery 6 V, fuse 6 V, cable 0 V, lamp 0 V. Transfer: every supply point 6 V while the lamp stays dark; with power isolated the lamp reports open continuity. Record the pair or component test that distinguishes your explanation before choosing a replacement. After the supported correction every lamp supply reads 6 V and the lamp lights.</p></details><p>6 V battery → fuse → cable → lamp → return. One component is open. A supply fault removes voltage downstream; a failed lamp can still receive 6 V. Isolate before continuity tests or replacement.</p><p>Use a facilitator to reveal requested readings from the campus pack. Compare adjacent powered points, or test the isolated component. Record an explanation that distinguishes an upstream fault from the component you propose to replace. After a supported replacement, measure lamp supply again and observe whether it lights. For independent browser practice, use the labelled measurement controls; the fault is not named in the briefing.</p><p>A working lamp by itself does not demonstrate diagnosis. An isolated supply reading of zero does not identify the original fault.</p></>}
    {week===6&&<><h3>Supplied file collection</h3><ul>{archiveFiles.map(f=><li><strong>{f.name}, {f.time}.</strong> {f.body}</li>)}</ul><p>Practice and check signed manifest: 24 sections, M-42. Transfer amended manifest: authorised annotated copy, 24 sections, M-99. Compare two or more records and justify your selection.</p><p><strong>Explanation:</strong> A meets the original manifest; B meets the amendment. C is incomplete. Preserve the prior source rather than silently overwriting it when the requirement changes.</p></>}
    {week===7&&<><h3>Supplied access model</h3><p>Observer: read. Technician: read and service. Registrar: read and certify. Initial faulty policy allows observer read, service and certify; technician and registrar have only read. Write a 3×3 permission table and mark all allowed and denied actions.</p><p>Transfer update: maintenance freeze suspends technician service. All other rules remain. Verify both that forbidden actions fail and permitted actions still work.</p><p><strong>Explanation:</strong> remove observer service/certify; enable technician service and registrar certify. Under the freeze, remove technician service again. Nine checks should match the published rules.</p></>}
    {week===8&&<><h3>Supplied role cards</h3><p>Analyst practice card: two sealed units, Relay, code AMBER. Check: three units, Archive, COPPER. Transfer: one unit, Dispatch, IVORY. Operator card: destinations Relay/Archive/Dispatch, batch sizes one/two/three; request exact instructions.</p><p>Work as a pair or switch roles. Compose the handoff, have the operator read back all three fields and record the analyst’s confirmation. Explain how you repaired an ambiguous instruction.</p><p><strong>Explanation:</strong> agreement requires matching destination, quantity and code plus acknowledgement; the sender’s confidence alone is insufficient.</p></>}
    {week===9&&<><h3>Negotiate explicit terms</h3><ul>{councilClaims.map(c=><li><strong>{c.speaker}:</strong> “{c.claim}” <br/>{c.record}</li>)}</ul><p>Protect provenance and restore service, or negotiate a recorded deferral. Choose a verified copy now, monitored stabilisation until review, or a supported-original move next shift. Every proposal needs recorded custody and independent verification. Match responsibility to the proposal: receiver, monitor, or custodian escort with certified support. An unsupported immediate move exceeds capacity.</p><p>Check mandate: original stays on site today. Transfer mandate: original provenance is essential; a copy alone is insufficient. Find two feasible agreements under the current mandate, describe each cost, and explain the concession you recommend. Feasibility is checked; fairness and reasoning require human review.</p></>}
    {week===10&&<><h3>Objective-led route planning</h3><p>Draw a 5×5 grid. Start row 5, column 1; destination row 1, column 5. Practice sensors: row 3, columns 1–4. Check: column 2, rows 2–5. Transfer: column 4, rows 2–5.</p><p>Choose fast dispatch (arrive within eight moves), support (visit centre row 3, column 3) or survey (visit two different sensor cells). Predict entries into marked cells, execute the route and compare. Each entry counts, including repeats. Choose and compare a route for another objective: fewer contacts do not necessarily serve the mission better.</p></>}
    {week===11&&<><h3>Preserved Version 1</h3><p>{initialPlan.join(' → ')}</p><p>Practice/check disruption: east passage blocked; west passage remains available but needs an extra relay check. Transfer disruption: meter unavailable; recorded readings battery 6 V, fuse 6 V, cable 0 V, lamp 0 V remain available.</p><p>Write Version 2 separately. Assign the additional check, explain the changed dependency and state what remains uncertain. Retain Version 1 so that the effect of the new evidence is visible. Select the replacement dependency (west relay for practice/check; reference readings for transfer) and rehearse it before activating Version 2. Written length only indicates that a record exists; a human must evaluate its quality.</p></>}
    {week===12&&<><h3>After-action worksheet</h3><p>Complete the mission via <a href={withBase('/operation/')}>Operation Last Light</a> or its published facilitator worksheet. Record the original objective, actual result, three consequential decisions, an unresolved limitation and a credible alternative. Attach the run record. This account does not replace practical evidence.</p></>}
    <h3>Reflection and example</h3><p>{lesson.exemplar}</p><p><strong>Your output:</strong> {lesson.output}. Record the conditions, actions, result and what you would test next. An explanation can be defensible while differing from the example.</p>
  </details>
  <noscript><p class="callout">The 3D and live controls require JavaScript. All supplied cases, rules, explanations and the complete worksheet above remain available. Record your answers in your own document and use the campus materials if preferred.</p></noscript>
</section>
<script>import '../scripts/training-client';</script>